\begin{frame}{Review of Previous Concepts}
  \begin{itemize}
    \item Robertson's theory: selection limit is $2N_e R(1)$, where $R(1)$ is first generation response.
    \item The limit depends on initial additive variance $\sigma_A^2(0)$ and effective population size $N_e$.
    \item Drift and selection jointly determine long-term response; increasing $N_e$ preserves more variation.
    \item Equation (26.15b) expressed the limit as $2N_e R(1) = N_e \bar{\imath} (2\sigma_A^2(0)/\sigma_z)$.
    \item Today we examine optimal selection intensity, population structure, and mutational input.
  \end{itemize}
\end{frame}

